# 4KFrame Enhanced — environment configuration.
# Copy this file to `.env` (which is gitignored) and fill in your values, then
# `docker compose up -d`. All values are optional; empty ones use the server defaults.

# --- Google Photos (Photo Picker API) ---
# Create an OAuth 2.0 "Web application" client in Google Cloud Console with the
# Photos Picker API enabled and the scope photospicker.mediaitems.readonly.
# NOTE: this needs an OAuth Client ID + Secret — NOT an API key.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must EXACTLY match an "Authorized redirect URI" on the OAuth client.
#   Docker on a LAN host:  http://<frame-host>:9095/api/google/callback
#   GitHub Codespace:      https://<codespace>-9095.app.github.dev/api/google/callback
#   Local dev:             http://localhost:9095/api/google/callback   (default if blank)
GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=

# --- Admin password (recommended, especially for any public/cloud host) ---
# When set, the admin UI and all management/control APIs require this password
# (the display/TV needs no login). Leave empty to keep the admin open (LAN only).
FRAME_ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# --- HTTPS (port 9096) ---
# Self-signed by default. To use your own cert, mount it into the container and set:
# FRAME_TLS_CERT=/data/cert.pem
# FRAME_TLS_KEY=/data/key.pem
# Set to 1 to turn HTTPS off entirely:
# FRAME_DISABLE_HTTPS=
